[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1195481247","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1195481247","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1195481247,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5HQZif","user":{"login":"dionhaefner","id":11994217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTk0MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11994217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner","html_url":"https://github.com/dionhaefner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-26T13:24:53Z","updated_at":"2022-07-26T13:24:53Z","body":"To reproduce you might have to use this branch of `mpi4jax`:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/mpi4jax/mpi4jax/pull/151","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1195481247/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1196090744","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1196090744","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1196090744,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5HSuV4","user":{"login":"sharadmv","id":1142926,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDI5MjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1142926?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv","html_url":"https://github.com/sharadmv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-26T23:27:34Z","updated_at":"2022-07-26T23:27:34Z","body":"I double checked the optimized HLO and it's still there:\r\nPre-compiled HLO\r\n```\r\nHloModule jit_send_jit.1, entry_computation_layout={(f32[10]{0})->f32[10]{0}}\r\n\r\nxla_fallback_send_mpi.3 {\r\n  constant.6 = s32[] constant(10)\r\n  Arg_0.4 = f32[10]{0} parameter(0)\r\n  constant.7 = s32[] constant(0)\r\n  constant.8 = u64[] constant(139673914379968)\r\n  constant.9 = u64[] constant(139673914351872)\r\n  Arg_1.5 = token[] parameter(1)\r\n  custom-call.10 = (token[]) custom-call(constant.6, Arg_0.4, constant.7, constant.7, constant.8, constant.9, Arg_1.5), custom_call_target=\"mpi_send\", custom_call_has_side_effect=true\r\n  ROOT get-tuple-element.11 = token[] get-tuple-element(custom-call.10), index=0\r\n}\r\n\r\nsend_mpi.12 {\r\n  Arg_0.13 = f32[10]{0} parameter(0)\r\n  Arg_1.14 = token[] parameter(1)\r\n  ROOT call.15 = token[] call(Arg_0.13, Arg_1.14), to_apply=xla_fallback_send_mpi.3\r\n}\r\n\r\nENTRY main.17 {\r\n  ROOT Arg_0.1 = f32[10]{0} parameter(0)\r\n  after-all.2 = token[] after-all()\r\n  call.16 = token[] call(Arg_0.1, after-all.2), to_apply=send_mpi.12\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nOptimized HLO:\r\n```\r\nHloModule jit_send_jit.2, entry_computation_layout={(f32[10]{0})->f32[10]{0}}\r\n\r\nENTRY %main.17 (Arg_0.1: f32[10]) -> f32[10] {\r\n  %constant.4 = s32[] constant(10)\r\n  %Arg_0.1 = f32[10]{0} parameter(0)\r\n  ROOT %copy = f32[10]{0} copy(f32[10]{0} %Arg_0.1)\r\n  %constant.5 = s32[] constant(0)\r\n  %constant.10 = u64[] constant(139673914379968)\r\n  %constant.11 = u64[] constant(139673914351872)\r\n  %after-all.2 = token[] after-all(), metadata={op_name=\"jit(send_jit)/jit(main)/create_token\" source_file=\"/usr/local/google/home/sharadmv/workspace/mpi4jax/mpi4jax/_src/collective_ops/send.py\" source_line=54}\r\n  %custom-call.1 = (token[]) custom-call(s32[] %constant.4, f32[10]{0} %copy, s32[] %constant.5, s32[] %constant.5, u64[] %constant.10, /*index=5*/u64[] %constant.11, token[] %after-all.2), custom_call_target=\"mpi_send\", custom_call_has_side_effect=true, metadata={op_name=\"custom-call.8\"}\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think this is an async issue (the Python program is ending before the message can happen).\r\n\r\nI was able to get it to show up in this repro:\r\n```python\r\nimport os\r\nos.environ[\"MPI4JAX_DEBUG\"] = \"1\"\r\n\r\nimport jax\r\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\r\n\r\nfrom mpi4py import MPI\r\nfrom mpi4jax import send\r\n\r\ncomm = MPI.COMM_WORLD\r\nassert comm.Get_size() == 1\r\n\r\n@jax.jit\r\ndef send_jit(x):\r\n    send(x, dest=0, comm=comm)\r\n    return x\r\n\r\n\r\nprint(\"send without JIT\")\r\nsend(jnp.ones(10), dest=0, comm=comm)\r\n\r\nprint(\"send with JIT\")\r\nsend_jit(jnp.ones(10)).block_until_ready()\r\n```\r\n\r\nOutput:\r\n```\r\nr0 | 9zBLijKJ | MPI_Send -> 0 with tag 0 and 10 items\r\nr0 | 9zBLijKJ | MPI_Send done with code 0 (2.90e-05s)\r\nsend with JIT\r\nr0 | LyW0FOeZ | MPI_Send -> 0 with tag 0 and 10 items\r\nr0 | LyW0FOeZ | MPI_Send done with code 0 (7.85e-06s)\r\n```","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1196090744/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1196387531","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1196387531","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1196387531,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5HT2zL","user":{"login":"dionhaefner","id":11994217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTk0MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11994217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner","html_url":"https://github.com/dionhaefner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-27T07:56:04Z","updated_at":"2022-07-27T07:56:04Z","body":"Huh. Actually, `mpi4jax` registers an `atexit` handler to prevent this kind of stuff:\r\n\r\n```python\r\ndef flush(platform):\r\n    \"\"\"Wait for all pending XLA operations\"\"\"\r\n    devices = jax.devices(platform)\r\n\r\n    for device in devices:\r\n        # as suggested in jax#4335\r\n        noop = jax.device_put(0, device=device) + 0\r\n        noop.block_until_ready()\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs that not sufficient anymore to wait for all async operations? 🤔 ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1196387531/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1199015401","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1199015401","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1199015401,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5Hd4Xp","user":{"login":"dionhaefner","id":11994217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTk0MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11994217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner","html_url":"https://github.com/dionhaefner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-29T08:28:43Z","updated_at":"2022-07-29T08:28:43Z","body":"That doesn't seem to be it. I get the same behavior even if I add a 10 second sleep in the end:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport os\r\nos.environ[\"MPI4JAX_DEBUG\"] = \"1\"\r\n\r\nimport jax\r\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\r\n\r\nfrom mpi4py import MPI\r\nfrom mpi4jax import send\r\n\r\ncomm = MPI.COMM_WORLD\r\nassert comm.Get_size() == 1\r\n\r\ndef flush(platform):\r\n    \"\"\"Wait for all pending XLA operations\"\"\"\r\n    devices = jax.devices(platform)\r\n\r\n    for device in devices:\r\n        # as suggested in jax#4335\r\n        noop = jax.device_put(0, device=device) + 0\r\n        noop.block_until_ready()\r\n\r\n# send to non-existing rank\r\n@jax.jit\r\ndef send_jit(x):\r\n    send(x, dest=0, comm=comm)\r\n\r\n\r\nprint(\"send without JIT\")\r\nsend(jnp.ones(10), dest=0, comm=comm)\r\n\r\nprint(\"send with JIT\")\r\nsend_jit(jnp.ones(10))\r\n\r\nimport time\r\ntime.sleep(10)\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1199015401/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1199019068","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1199019068","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1199019068,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5Hd5Q8","user":{"login":"dionhaefner","id":11994217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTk0MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11994217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner","html_url":"https://github.com/dionhaefner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-29T08:33:01Z","updated_at":"2022-07-29T08:33:01Z","body":"Actually, it works for any return argument that is not `None`:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# works\r\n@jax.jit\r\ndef send_jit(x):\r\n    send(x, dest=0, comm=comm)\r\n    return 0\r\n\r\n# nope\r\n@jax.jit\r\ndef send_jit(x):\r\n    send(x, dest=0, comm=comm)\r\n    return None\r\n```\r\n\r\nDo functions that don't return anything get optimized away since recently?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1199019068/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1199331120","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1199331120","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1199331120,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5HfFcw","user":{"login":"hawkinsp","id":348932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODkzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/348932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp","html_url":"https://github.com/hawkinsp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-29T14:02:42Z","updated_at":"2022-07-29T14:02:42Z","body":"I'm trying to run your repro but it just hangs for me.\r\n\r\nI did:\r\n```\r\n$ apt install libmpich-dev\r\n$ git clone https://github.com/mpi4jax/mpi4jax.git\r\n$ cd mpi4jax\r\n$ git fetch origin pull/151/head\r\n$ git checkout FETCH_HEAD\r\n$ pip install -e .\r\n```\r\n\r\nand then tried running your repro:\r\n```\r\n$ python m.py\r\nsend without JIT\r\nWARNING:absl:No GPU/TPU found, falling back to CPU. (Set TF_CPP_MIN_LOG_LEVEL=0 and rerun for more info.)\r\nr0 | yrpTbyMM | MPI_Send -> 0 with tag 0 and 10 items\r\n```\r\nAt this point it hangs apparently forever.\r\n\r\nWhat am I doing wrong?","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1199331120/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1199894523","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1199894523","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1199894523,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5HhO_7","user":{"login":"dionhaefner","id":11994217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTk0MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11994217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner","html_url":"https://github.com/dionhaefner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-29T19:49:25Z","updated_at":"2022-07-29T19:49:25Z","body":"Sorry, my bad. Because the example code sends without receiving, it will deadlock with many MPI providers.\r\n\r\nHere's one that should work for all setups:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport os\r\nos.environ[\"MPI4JAX_DEBUG\"] = \"1\"\r\n\r\nimport jax\r\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\r\n\r\nfrom mpi4py import MPI\r\nfrom mpi4jax import sendrecv\r\n\r\ncomm = MPI.COMM_WORLD\r\nassert comm.Get_size() == 1\r\n\r\n@jax.jit\r\ndef sendrecv_jit(x):\r\n    sendrecv(x, x, source=0, dest=0, comm=comm)\r\n\r\nprint(\"sendrecv without JIT\")\r\nsendrecv(jnp.ones(10), jnp.ones(10), source=0, dest=0, comm=comm)\r\n\r\nprint(\"sendrecv with JIT\")\r\nsendrecv_jit(jnp.ones(10))\r\n\r\nimport time\r\ntime.sleep(10)\r\n```\r\n\r\nOutput:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nsendrecv without JIT\r\nr0 | 05WTiqzD | MPI_Sendrecv <- 0 (tag -1, 10 items) / -> 0 (tag 0, 10 items)\r\nr0 | 05WTiqzD | MPI_Sendrecv done with code 0 (3.26e-05s)\r\nsendrecv with JIT\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter adding `return 0` to `sendrecv_jit`:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nsendrecv without JIT\r\nr0 | 05WTiqzD | MPI_Sendrecv <- 0 (tag -1, 10 items) / -> 0 (tag 0, 10 items)\r\nr0 | 05WTiqzD | MPI_Sendrecv done with code 0 (3.26e-05s)\r\nsendrecv with JIT\r\nr0 | XoGaYz72 | MPI_Sendrecv <- 0 (tag -1, 10 items) / -> 0 (tag 0, 10 items)\r\nr0 | XoGaYz72 | MPI_Sendrecv done with code 0 (3.92e-06s)\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1199894523/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1201176175","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1201176175","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1201176175,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5HmH5v","user":{"login":"hawkinsp","id":348932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0ODkzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/348932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp","html_url":"https://github.com/hawkinsp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hawkinsp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-01T13:05:34Z","updated_at":"2022-08-01T13:05:34Z","body":"@sharadmv I think the bug is here:\r\nhttps://github.com/google/jax/blob/c08b4ee6d9a13787c16bcf867d04e04d81fca063/jax/_src/dispatch.py#L329\r\n\r\nnote that `jaxpr.outvars` is empty, and a custom call with a side effect isn't considered to have a `jaxpr` effect. I suspect we need to treat effectful custom calls as effectful for `jaxpr` purposes as well?","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1201176175/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1201809647","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1201809647","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1201809647,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5Hoijv","user":{"login":"sharadmv","id":1142926,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDI5MjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1142926?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv","html_url":"https://github.com/sharadmv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-01T22:49:14Z","updated_at":"2022-08-01T22:50:04Z","body":"I see. You need to define your primitives to be effectful. To do that, use:\r\n```python\r\neffect = <some hashable>\r\ndef _effectful_abstract_eval(...):\r\n  return ..., {effect}\r\nprim.def_effectful_abstract_eval(_effectful_abstract_eval)\r\nfrom jax.interpreters import mlir\r\nfrom jax._src.lax import control_flow as lcf\r\n\r\nmlir.lowerable_effects.add(effect)\r\nlcf.allowable_effects.add(effect)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis will automatically make any jaxpr that contains these primitives have an effect and we will bypass the check that Peter mentioned.\r\n\r\nAn added benefit will be that you no longer need to use your `atexit` handler. Instead you can call `jax.effects_barrier()` which does the same thing.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1201809647/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1202201365","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1202201365","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1202201365,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5HqCMV","user":{"login":"dionhaefner","id":11994217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTk0MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11994217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner","html_url":"https://github.com/dionhaefner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-02T08:49:07Z","updated_at":"2022-08-02T08:49:07Z","body":"That seems to work, thanks. \r\n\r\nWhat are the semantics of the `effect` object? Can I re-use the same object for all primitives?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1202201365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1203021861","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1203021861","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1203021861,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5HtKgl","user":{"login":"sharadmv","id":1142926,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDI5MjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1142926?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv","html_url":"https://github.com/sharadmv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-02T17:33:27Z","updated_at":"2022-08-02T17:33:27Z","body":"The effect object can be any hashable (internally we use enums usually). It functions as tag that shows up in jaxprs (in `jaxpr.effects`). You can re-use it for whichever primitives you want this blocking behavior for.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1203021861/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1204297326","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1204297326","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1204297326,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5HyB5u","user":{"login":"PhilipVinc","id":2407108,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MDcxMDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2407108?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc","html_url":"https://github.com/PhilipVinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-03T17:59:18Z","updated_at":"2022-08-03T17:59:18Z","body":"@sharadmv Would it be posssible to make `from jax._src.lax import control_flow as lcf` part of the public/exported API? We have several users and would like to avoid `mpi4jax` breaking too often because we rely on internal things.\r\n\r\nIf this is part of the API necessary to define custom effectfull primitives, then it might make sense to have it in the public API. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1204297326/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1204315911","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1204315911","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1204315911,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5HyGcH","user":{"login":"sharadmv","id":1142926,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDI5MjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1142926?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv","html_url":"https://github.com/sharadmv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-03T18:16:40Z","updated_at":"2022-08-03T18:16:40Z","body":"The custom effectful primitive API is considered internal and experimental and will likely change in the future. We can't at the moment promise a public, stable interface. Using custom JAX primitives is also technically internal / unstable (although probably less likely to dramatically change than the new effects system).\r\n\r\nI initially recommended an unstable solution because I was under the impression that `mpi4jax` was okay being broken by JAX internal changes given the existing dependence on primitives.\r\n\r\nAn alternate, stable solution would be to do manual token threading (this is what the effects system current does underneath the hood) and to block on the output tokens:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n@jax.jit\r\ndef sendrecv_jit(token, x):\r\n    sendrecv(x, x, source=0, dest=0, comm=comm)\r\n    return token\r\n```\r\n\r\n`token` can be something as simple as a zero-length array (`np.zeros(0, np.bool_)` for example) and is just needed to block on the computation. You can look at [this design note](https://jax.readthedocs.io/en/latest/design_notes/sequencing_effects.html) which informed the current effect system's design.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1204315911/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1204330807","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1204330807","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1204330807,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5HyKE3","user":{"login":"dionhaefner","id":11994217,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTk0MjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11994217?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner","html_url":"https://github.com/dionhaefner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dionhaefner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-03T18:31:42Z","updated_at":"2022-08-03T18:31:42Z","body":"@sharadmv Thanks for the clarification. We actually already do token threading to enforce order of our primitives, and it's sort of a major pain. So this piqued my interest:\r\n\r\n> An alternate, stable solution would be to do manual token threading (this is what the effects system current does underneath the hood)\r\n\r\nSo the effects system actually does automated token tracking? In this case we could just abandon our manual token threading, which would be amazing. But kind of hard to depend on if this is an unstable feature... 🤔 ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1204330807/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1204333811","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1204333811","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1204333811,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5HyKzz","user":{"login":"PhilipVinc","id":2407108,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MDcxMDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2407108?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc","html_url":"https://github.com/PhilipVinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-03T18:34:44Z","updated_at":"2022-08-03T18:34:44Z","body":">An alternate, stable solution would be to do manual token threading (this is what the effects system current does underneath the hood) and to block on the output tokens:\r\n\r\nThis is not really an option right now because we'd have to force users to weave tokens themselves in and out of jitted functions, which we are severely trying to avoid.\r\n\r\n>The custom effectful primitive API is considered internal and experimental and will likely change in the future. We can't at the moment promise a public, stable interface. Using custom JAX primitives is also technically internal / unstable (although probably less likely to dramatically change than the new effects system).\r\n\r\nAh, ok. We have several downstream users so we try to rely on as stable APIs as possible. The current iteration of `mpi4jax` has persisted practically unbroken for 12+ months (if not for reshuffling of your API entry points), and I would be happy if this could continue.\r\n\r\nI was under the impression that `jax.core` is part of the public API, and since `jax.core.Primitive` is there as well I expected that to be stable. This is why I asked to make `control_flow` stable as well. \r\nBut if that's not the case it's good to know. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1204333811/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1204660718","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1204660718","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1204660718,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5Hzanu","user":{"login":"sharadmv","id":1142926,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDI5MjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1142926?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv","html_url":"https://github.com/sharadmv","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sharadmv/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-08-04T01:37:53Z","updated_at":"2022-08-04T01:37:53Z","body":"> I was under the impression that jax.core is part of the public API, and since jax.core.Primitive is there as well I expected that to be stable. This is why I asked to make control_flow stable as well.\r\n\r\nThe official list of public modules [is available here](https://jax.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api_compatibility.html).\r\n\r\n> Ah, ok. We have several downstream users so we try to rely on as stable APIs as possible. The current iteration of mpi4jax has persisted practically unbroken for 12+ months (if not for reshuffling of your API entry points), and I would be happy if this could continue.\r\n\r\nIs it possible to release `mpi4jax` versions with pinned JAX/jaxlibs?","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1204660718/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1204888392","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620#issuecomment-1204888392","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/11620","id":1204888392,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5H0SNI","user":{"login":"dionhaefner","id":119